From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Paul Golmann <684458+pjeweb@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 22 Nov 2026 16:34:16 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 53/57] hwmon: pwm-fan: read shutdown duty before registering cleanup

A tach IRQ request can fail after PWM setup. Load the firmware shutdown
duty before registering cleanup so probe unwind uses the configured duty.

First-party: authored by CeraLive against v7.2, with no upstream
counterpart in rockchip-rk3588-mainline-patches. The source of record
is ceralive/0053-hwmon-pwm-fan-read-shutdown-duty-early.patch
and patches/ is generated from it by scripts/build-series.py.
scripts/verify-payload-parity.py holds it to the same
added/removed-line parity the upstream lane gets.

Intended for upstream review on linux-hwmon.
Submission and DCO sign-off are separate from this integration.

---
diff --git a/drivers/hwmon/pwm-fan.c b/drivers/hwmon/pwm-fan.c
index 37f3781..dd0fe37 100644
--- a/drivers/hwmon/pwm-fan.c
+++ b/drivers/hwmon/pwm-fan.c
@@ -555,6 +555,12 @@ static int pwm_fan_probe(struct platform_device *pdev)
 	if (ret)
 		return ret;
 
+	/* Cleanup can run on a probe error after PWM setup. */
+	ret = device_property_read_u32(dev, "fan-shutdown-percent",
+				       &pwm_shutdown_percent);
+	if (!ret && pwm_shutdown_percent)
+		ctx->pwm_shutdown = (clamp(pwm_shutdown_percent, 0, 100) * 255) / 100;
+
 	/* use maximum cooling level if provided */
 	if (ctx->pwm_fan_cooling_levels)
 		initial_pwm = ctx->pwm_fan_cooling_levels[ctx->pwm_fan_max_state];
@@ -654,11 +660,6 @@ static int pwm_fan_probe(struct platform_device *pdev)
 		channels[1] = &ctx->fan_channel;
 	}
 
-	ret = device_property_read_u32(dev, "fan-shutdown-percent",
-				       &pwm_shutdown_percent);
-	if (!ret && pwm_shutdown_percent)
-		ctx->pwm_shutdown = (clamp(pwm_shutdown_percent, 0, 100) * 255) / 100;
-
 	ret = device_property_read_u32(dev, "fan-stop-to-start-percent",
 				       &pwm_min_from_stopped);
 	if (!ret && pwm_min_from_stopped) {
